# 🛡️ Analytics Rules

Microsoft Sentinel was configured with custom scheduled analytics rules to detect a wide range of attacker techniques across the MITRE ATT&CK framework. These detections leverage Windows Security Events, Sysmon logs, and custom KQL queries collected through Azure Monitor Agent (AMA) and Data Collection Rules (DCRs).

Each rule is designed to identify suspicious or malicious activity, generate an alert, create an incident, and trigger automated response workflows through Microsoft Sentinel.

---

## Analytics Rule Summary

| Detection Rule | Severity | MITRE ATT&CK | Description |
|---------------|----------|--------------|-------------|
| **[Brute Force Login Detection](#-brute-force-login-detection)** | High | T1110 | Detects repeated failed Windows logon attempts. |
| **[Successful Login After Brute Force](#-successful-login-after-brute-force)** | High | T1078 | Detects a successful authentication following multiple failed login attempts. |
| **[New Local User Creation](#-new-local-user-creation)** | Medium | T1136 | Detects creation of new local user accounts. |
| **[Encoded PowerShell Detection](#-encoded-powershell-detection)** | High | T1059.001 | Detects Base64 encoded PowerShell commands. |
| **[Download Cradle Detection](#-download-cradle-detection)** | High | T1105 | Detects PowerShell downloading payloads from remote sources. |
| **[Mimikatz Detection](#-mimikatz-detection)** | High | T1003 | Detects execution of the Mimikatz credential dumping tool. |
| **[PsExec Detection](#-psexec-detection)** | High | T1021.002 | Detects PsExec-based remote execution and lateral movement. |
| **[Registry Run Key Persistence](#-registry-run-key-persistence)** | High | T1547.001 | Detects persistence through Windows Run Registry Keys. |
| **[Event Log Cleared Detection](#-event-log-cleared-detection)** | High | T1070.001 | Detects attempts to clear Windows Event Logs. |
| **[New Windows Service Installed](#-new-windows-service-installed)** | High | T1543.003 | Detects installation of new Windows services. |
| **[Scheduled Task Creation](#-scheduled-task-creation)** | Medium | T1053.005 | Detects scheduled tasks created for persistence or execution. |
| **[Suspicious Discovery Commands](#-suspicious-discovery-commands)** | Medium | T1082 / T1016 / T1033 | Detects common reconnaissance commands executed by attackers. |
| **[Domain Admin Group Modification](#-domain-admin-group-modification)** | Critical | T1098 | Detects additions to privileged Active Directory groups. |
